  <h1>Why This Matters</h1>
  <p>AI assistants are becoming the place where your thinking happens — research, planning, writing, debugging, learning, and long threads of reasoning. But none of them give you real ownership.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ChatGPT stores everything in the cloud</li>
    <li>Claude's Projects live behind an account</li>
    <li>Perplexity deletes history after 30 days</li>
    <li>Gemini requires Google Takeout</li>
    <li>Grok keeps everything online</li>
    <li>DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen Chat all lock history behind their own web sessions</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your work is scattered across eight companies, eight UIs, and eight histories that can change at any time.</p>
  <p>TotalRecalls gives you a single, durable archive you control.</p>
  <p>A folder of Markdown on your disk still opens in ten years. It survives account changes, UI redesigns, pricing shifts, and platform churn.</p>
  <p><strong>Your conversations become files — not tabs.</strong></p>
  <p>This is why TotalRecalls exists.</p>
</PageLayout>
